{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Not because you are numerous.</b> Rashbam would join this verse with the first verse of ״והיה״ and explain thus: ״לא מרבכם חשק ה' בכם״ — not because of your multitude did HaShem desire you, but rather ״מאהבת ה' אתכם ומשמרו את השבועה״ — from HaShem's love for you and His keeping of the oath. And if you ask: since He desired us only by force of the oath, why should we exert ourselves to keep His commandments? Therefore it is written: ״וידעת כי ה' אלהיך הוא אלהי האלהים״ etc. — ״שומר הברית״: He awaits the covenant of the oath and the kindness, until He finds those who love Him and keep His commandments, ״לאלף דור״ — that is, up to a thousand generations He waits, until He finds a worthy generation, keepers of the commandments, to receive the reward of the oath that He swore to our fathers."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:34.708631803Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}